Description: Let the server keep drawing a closing window while it fades out
 Umoja animates windows opening and minimizing by fading and scaling their
 scene surface, but a closing window's surface left the scene the moment
 the client destroyed it, so there was nothing to animate. If the server
 executable exports a C function named mir_surface_linger_hook, the
 surface stack asks it when removing a surface whether to keep drawing it
 (non-zero). Such a surface leaves the stack as usual (no input, observers
 told it is gone) but is still drawn on top of its old layer, and the
 stack is asked again at each scene until it answers 0. Alpha and
 transformation changes on it redraw the scene. Compositors the scene
 filter hook (3018) speaks for don't show it. Without the hook nothing
 changes; no ABI change.
Author: Umoja developers
Forwarded: no

